$ run_shell git log -n 1 --pretty=format:%B tests/test_voice_polish.py
Fix test/fixture drift surfaced by isolated self-update validation

Three stale expectations in the suite, all from intentional behavior
changes that outpaced their tests:

- Voice capacity notices: _StubState lacked _notice_last and two tests
  still asserted pre-cooldown semantics. Commit 62a43c10 added a
  10-minute family cooldown specifically to stop flap narration —
  deeper cuts and oscillation inside the window now correctly stay
  silent. Tests updated to assert the cooldown contract.
- Lightweight utility route: two workflow tests used repository-summary
  prompts that the deterministic github_read lane now answers locally,
  so the model provider was never invoked. Prompts changed to exercise
  the path each test actually targets (question prompt for the clock/
  prefix-cache assertion; action prompt for the tool-schema check).
- server.py: removed dead-code route stubs left over from the Phase A
  route relocation — they tripped the route-coverage lint.

